From 326879073f595e564e3a123e9627d64c7d04f5a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:26:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 18/22] drm/gma500: copy rectangles on the SGX545

Add dri/N/sgx/xfer_copy: a one-layer FASTSCALE transfer that fetches a linear
ARGB8888 source rectangle as a texture and writes it through the PBE. Fill and
copy now each have their own program placement, and share the command, kick
and completion checks. Three cases (a whole surface, an offset rectangle
between differently padded strides, a rectangle across tiles) are checked on
every destination dword against a source pattern in which every byte varies;
all are exact on the GMA3600.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
